sources.update({
 'setfit':('Hugging Face, SetFit documentation','https://huggingface.co/docs/setfit/main/index'),
 'sklearn':('scikit-learn, text classification examples','https://scikit-learn.org/stable/auto_examples/text/index.html'),
 'qwen':('Qwen, structured output with vLLM','https://qwen.readthedocs.io/en/v3.0/deployment/vllm.html')})
original=slides[:]
slides=[]
def keep(i): slides.append(original[i-1])
add('Jev and classifiers<br>in agentic banking','<p class="hero">What they are, where they fit and how they help</p><p class="sub">An introduction for business and IT</p><p class="meta">40-minute session · 29 September 2026</p>','Timing: 1 minute. The topic is adopting Jev and other models as classifiers within banking agent architectures. This is an introductory session, not a vendor selection or a proposal to train a foundation model. Plan 35 minutes of presentation and five minutes of discussion.',kind='cover')
add('Today’s discussion',rows(['Time','Topic','Question'],[['8 minutes','The basic idea','What does a classifier add to an agent?'],['10 minutes','Banking examples','Where can it improve a workflow?'],['12 minutes','Architecture and model choices','How does IT integrate and evaluate it?'],['5 minutes','Adoption','What would a sensible first step look like?'],['5 minutes','Discussion','Where does this fit in our bank?']]),'Timing: 1 minute. These section timings include the opening. Use the appendices only if questions require more depth. Avoid explaining the mathematics before the customer example.')
add('An agent carries out a workflow',split('<p class="statement">A banking agent uses context and tools to work toward a defined objective.</p>',points(['Understand the request.','Gather permitted information.','Choose and execute allowed steps.','Check the result or ask for help.']))+'<p class="callout">Example: investigate a card dispute, collect evidence and prepare a case for review.</p>','Timing: 1.5 minutes. This is a working definition. A chatbot mainly exchanges messages. An agent may also retrieve records, update a case or call a service. Autonomy varies by workflow. The bank chooses which actions are available and which require approval.')
add('A classifier answers a bounded question',split('<p class="quote">“I don’t recognise this card payment.”</p><p>The available labels might be card dispute, payment status, account access or other.</p>','<p class="eyebrow">Illustrative classification</p><p class="statement">card_dispute</p><p>The workflow uses this label to choose the next process.</p>'))
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 1.5 minutes. Classification maps an input to a defined category. Some models also return probabilities or multiple independent flags. A classifier can process a message, a document excerpt or the state of a workflow. The label set is a business design decision.'
keep(4)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 2 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
keep(5)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 1 minute. '+slides[-1]['notes']
add('Why put a classifier inside an agent?',rows(['Workflow need','Classifier contribution','Business outcome to measure'],[['Understand varied customer language','Map messages to known intents','Fewer avoidable transfers'],['Spot cases needing attention','Flag urgency or missing evidence','Earlier specialist review'],['Choose a suitable processing path','Route simple and complex work separately','Lower cost or faster completion'],['Check an intermediate result','Assess relevance or completeness','Less rework']])+'<p class="sub">Potential benefits depend on measured model performance and the surrounding workflow.</p>','Timing: 1 minute. These are candidate benefits, not guaranteed improvements. A wrong classifier can add transfers, delays or missed cases. The useful unit of measurement is the completed business process. A classifier call adds cost and latency too, so use it only where it improves the complete flow.')
keep(6)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 2 minutes. Ask the audience which queue they would choose. Then reveal the multiple signals: dispute, possible fraud, financial pressure and missing transaction evidence. Do not interpret rent urgency alone as proof of vulnerability. This is an illustrative scenario, not actual model output.'
add('The same message, two possible paths',split('<h3>Clear and supported</h3>'+points(['Classify the intent.','Fetch authorised transaction details.','Apply the bank’s dispute procedure.','Prepare the specialist case.']),'<h3>Ambiguous or incomplete</h3>'+points(['Ask a focused clarification.','Avoid guessing the transaction.','Route to a person when needed.','Record the handoff and reason.']))+'<p class="callout">The classifier changes the route. The bank’s workflow controls the action.</p>','Timing: 2 minutes. Walk through both paths using the same customer request. An agent may collect facts and prepare a case, but refunds, card blocking and customer notifications require their own permissions. Re-run relevant judgments when material context changes, and limit loops and retries.')
add('Example: onboarding evidence',split('<p class="quote">A business customer uploads a registration document and an address letter.</p>','<h3>Classifier tasks</h3>'+points(['Identify each document type.','Assess relevance to the requested evidence.','Flag inconsistency for review.']))+'<p class="callout">Useful outcome: a clearer missing-evidence checklist and fewer repeated requests.</p>','Timing: 1.5 minutes. This is a proposed workflow. OCR or a multimodal component may first extract text; the cited Jev interface accepts text/state rather than images. Authoritative checks still establish identity and regulatory sufficiency. Document classification cannot establish authenticity. Measure rework and overlooked evidence, not just category accuracy.',('do',))
add('Example: a relationship manager’s assistant',split('<p class="quote">“Prepare the client’s annual credit review.”</p>','<h3>Classifier tasks</h3>'+points(['Select relevant retrieved passages.','Identify evidence gaps.','Route unsupported draft claims for review.']))+'<p class="sub">DBS reported an agentic credit-memo drafting rollout to about 1,500 staff in August 2026. It is an adoption example, not evidence that DBS uses Jev.</p>','Timing: 1.5 minutes. The proposed classifier roles are our architecture examples. DBS describes specialised agents preparing review-ready memo drafts and human bankers deepening the assessment. Do not attribute our classifier architecture or Jev usage to DBS. Credit approval remains a separate governed decision.',('dbs',))
keep(7)
slides[-1]['title']='Where classifiers can help first'
slides[-1]['body']=slides[-1]['body'].replace('Service triage · pilot','Service triage').replace('Initial authority','Possible starting scope').replace('Proposed sequence.','Illustrative portfolio.')
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 2 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
keep(8)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 2 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
keep(9)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 1.5 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
add('Jev is one option in a broader toolkit',rows(['Approach','How it classifies','Main consideration'],[['Jev / System One','Typed questions against supplied state','Validate native probabilities on bank cases'],['Text features + linear classifier','Learns labels from labelled text','Useful baseline for stable taxonomies'],['Sentence Transformer / SetFit','Embeddings plus a trained classification head','Needs representative labels and calibration'],['LLM with constrained output, e.g. Qwen','Prompts map context to allowed output labels','Valid JSON does not establish correctness']])+'<p class="sub">These are candidate approaches, not a ranked benchmark.</p>','Timing: 2 minutes. Jev supports Choice, Score and Noul. SetFit is a framework for adapting Sentence Transformers with a classifier. scikit-learn documents sparse text classification. Qwen documents structured outputs using vLLM. These approaches differ in training, serving and output semantics. Do not equate a framework with a model checkpoint or make unsupported claims that one is fastest or cheapest.',('jev','setfit','sklearn','qwen'))
add('The right choice depends on the workflow',rows(['Situation','Options worth testing'],[['Stable labels and enough historical examples','Conventional classifier or a fine-tuned encoder'],['Questions change and labelled data are limited','Jev-style typed questions or a prompted LLM'],['Long, ambiguous evidence requires reasoning','Reasoning model with bounded checks and human escalation'],['Data must remain in a controlled environment','Approved deployment of a suitable licensed model']])+'<p class="callout">Compare accuracy, calibration, latency, total cost and deployment fit on the same cases.</p>','Timing: 1.5 minutes. This table is a design heuristic, not a performance claim. Data availability, language, licensing and hosting constraints can reverse the choice. Verify vendor residency, retention, model versioning, SLA and exit arrangements. No claim is made that Jev supports an on-premise deployment.')
keep(10)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 1.5 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
keep(11)
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 1.5 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
keep(14)
slides[-1]['title']='How the bank knows it is helping'
slides[-1]['notes']='Timing: 2 minutes. '+slides[-1]['notes']
add('Benefits appear in the whole workflow',split('<h3>Business measures</h3>'+points(['Time to the correct queue.','Staff time spent on avoidable rework.','Urgent cases found and missed.','Customer completion and complaints.']),'<h3>IT measures</h3>'+points(['Cost per successful case.','End-to-end response time.','Model and service failure rates.','Manual fallback and recovery.']))+'<p class="callout">A cheaper model call has little value if it creates more manual work.</p>','Timing: 1.5 minutes. Compare against the current workflow, including staff time, review and exception costs. Separate released capacity from realised cash savings. Measure before and after with comparable cases and clear denominators. Avoid importing vendor benchmark speed or price ratios into a banking ROI claim.')
add('A practical way to begin',rows(['Step','What the team learns'],[['Choose one narrow workflow','Which judgment causes friction today?'],['Compare candidates offline','Can a classifier improve on existing routing?'],['Run alongside staff','Does performance hold on real incoming cases?'],['Allow limited routing with a fallback','Does the entire workflow improve safely?']])+'<p class="sub">Business defines the outcome and exceptions. IT provides integration and measurement. Risk teams challenge the evidence.</p>','Timing: 1 minute. This is a possible adoption path, not a budget request. Start with an existing manual process and clear ownership. Keep customer-impacting actions under existing authorisation. Expand only after evidence supports it. Timelines depend on data access, integration and review.')
add('What to remember', '<p class="statement">Classifiers give agents usable judgments at specific points in a workflow.</p>'+points(['Jev packages those judgments as typed outputs with probabilities.','Other classification models can fill the same architectural role.','Bank policy, validation and operations determine whether the result is useful.']), 'Timing: 1 minute. The main concept is a bounded judgment service within a larger banking architecture. A model output can inform the next step, while the bank retains control over execution. No classifier is automatically suitable for every banking decision.')
add('Discussion', '<p class="statement">Where does a small judgment create a large amount of manual work in our bank?</p>'+points(['Which decision repeats most often?','What evidence would convince us to use a classifier?','Which actions must always remain under explicit approval?']), 'Timing: 5 minutes. Capture candidate workflows and the decision owner. Keep the conversation on narrow judgments that can be labelled and evaluated. Use the appendix if the discussion turns to financial value, data quality or controls.')
for i in [13,15,20]:
    keep(i)
    slides[-1]['title']='Appendix: '+slides[-1]['title'].replace('Appendix: ','')
    slides[-1]['notes']='Optional appendix; outside the 40-minute running order. '+slides[-1]['notes']
add('Appendix: sources', '<div class="sources">'+''.join('<p><a href="'+u+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">'+html.escape(t)+'</a></p>' for k,(t,u) in sources.items() if k in ['jev','do','dbs','cal','setfit','sklearn','qwen'])+'</div>','Sources reviewed 29 September 2026. Vendor documentation supports interface and implementation descriptions, not independent banking performance. DBS supplies a bank-reported adoption example. All workflow examples, integration recommendations and economic assumptions are illustrative. No model was trained or benchmarked for this presentation.')
